    dHf_298
    {
        origin        derived;
        method        "ab initio composite (ANL0) enthalpy of formation at 0 K, as printed in the cited journal paper for n-C4H3 (CHCHCCH), converted to 298.15 K with this tool's own thermal enthalpies";
        methodVersion "Klippenstein, Harding & Ruscic, J. Phys. Chem. A 121 (2017) 6580-6602, doi:10.1021/acs.jpca.7b05945, Table 2, manuscript PDF page 35 of the accepted manuscript at OSTI 1389058";
        inputs
        (
            { quantity "Delta_f H at 0 K (ANL0 ab initio CALCULATED, not ATcT, paper label CHCHCCH, Table 2; +-2.2 kJ/mol)"; value 547.4; unit kJ/mol; doi "10.1021/acs.jpca.7b05945"; }
        );
        uncertainty   "+-2.2 kJ/mol (twice the 1.08 kJ/mol RMS error of the same ANL0 method against 150 ATcT species, Table 4 of the paper)";
        notes         "n-C4H3 (H-C#C-CH=CH, the isomer formed by 2 C2H2 = C4H3 + H, reaction A122) is NOT in the ATcT species set of that paper: its Table 2 lists the ANL0 CALCULATED Delta_f H(0 K) = 547.4 kJ/mol for CHCHCCH, and this record uses that calculated value, not an ATcT value (the earlier record cited ATcT 1.124 by version only, which is no source). The 298.15 K value is DERIVED: Delta_f H(0) + [H(298.15)-H(0)] of the species (rrho_thermo.py) - sum of the elements' increments (CODATA Key Values: C graphite 1.050, H2 8.468 kJ/mol), net increment -2.328 kJ/mol. The value held before 2026-11-23 (544.74, website version) lies 0.33 kJ/mol from it. The resonance-stabilised i-C4H3 (H2C=C=C=CH, 495.7 at 0 K in the same table) is lower in energy and is NOT used.";
    }
